######################
# Workspace root
#
# The Spring Boot application keeps JHipster's comprehensive .gitignore inside backend/,
# and git honours an ignore file in every directory it covers — so everything under
# backend/ (its target/, node_modules/, logs, IDE files) is already handled there. This
# file only has to deal with what sits beside it: the frontend, the editor workspace, and
# the clutter an operating system leaves behind.
######################

######################
# Frontend
######################
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-store/

######################
# Editor workspace
#
# The four files below are committed on purpose: they carry the shared formatter, compiler
# and launch settings, and leaving them out means every machine configures this project
# differently. Everything else VS Code writes here is local state.
######################
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.code-workspace

.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
.classpath
.project
.settings/

######################
# Logs and temporary files
######################
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*~

######################
# Operating system
######################
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
